# Zilar nightly backup (Docker Compose install).
#
# Least-invasive schedule for the Compose path: no extra container, no
# Docker socket mount — one host cron line running the install helper.
# (A `backup` sidecar container would need the Docker socket to reach the
# database containers, which widens what a compromised backup job can do;
# the helper already talks to the stack through the local docker CLI.)
#
# Install as the user that owns the checkout (root only if the checkout
# is root-owned), with the checkout path filled in:
#
#   crontab -e
#
# Every night at 03:30. --keep 7 retains the newest 7 archives in
# deploy/backups/ (0600, live secrets inside). doctor warns when the
# newest backup is older than 2 days, so a silent cron failure surfaces
# the next time anyone runs `./deploy/zilar doctor`:
#
#   30 3 * * * /opt/zilar/deploy/zilar backup --keep 7 >>/var/log/zilar-backup.log 2>&1
#
# Off-machine copy (a backup on the same disk is not a backup): encrypt
# first, then copy. `./deploy/zilar backup --offsite-hint` prints the
# exact commands for the newest archive (age/gpg + scp, or rclone).
#
# After editing, confirm the line is installed and the helper runs:
#
#   crontab -l | grep zilar
#   /opt/zilar/deploy/zilar backup --dry-run
